# Not hygiene -- a correctness and speed requirement.
# Without this, `COPY . .` in the builder stage sweeps in the host's
# target/ (easily 1-3 GB with debug artifacts) and any worktrees living
# under .claude/, which both bloats the image and invalidates layer
# caching on every build, since those paths churn constantly.
#
# Do not over-exclude: the builder needs Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/,
# and tests/. README.md, DECISIONS.md, and .port-mortem.toml are COPY'd
# explicitly into the parity stage, so they must not be ignored here.

# Build outputs -- large, and they churn on every local build
target/
**/node_modules/
tests/.work/

# Agent worktrees live inside the repo; never bake one into the image
.claude/worktrees/

# VCS and editor state
.git/
.idea/
*.swp

# Generated evidence: belongs in the repo, not baked into the image
fuzz/corpus/
proptest-regressions/
bench/raw/

# Planning docs the image has no use for
